and now we were just talking with  brandon lewis among other things about  the campaign for the footballer  marcus rashford to get the government to  provide free school meals to the poorest  children  over half term and other school holidays  as well this week mps voted against  doing that but label wants that to be  another vote  we're joined now by the shadow mental  health minister dr rosanna  alain khan thank you very much for being  with us thank you for having me  so you're going to be pushing for  another vote on this what's the plan  absolutely the labour party are not  going to give up on our young people on  the children who are going to bed hungry  and the fact that 322 mps made the  morally reprehensible decision to vote  against free school meals this week is  deeply suddenly but i will say  that what has played out over the  ensuing days  is the very best of what it means to be  british our communities have stood up to  this government and say  and said we don't care what you have  done we  are angry and we are going to take  matters into our own hands and so we  have seen  you know local restaurants communities  councils  stepping up even though so many  themselves have been hit so hard by this  covert crisis  and providing support for children and  young people  and it makes me so proud to be british  and i know that marcus rashford and his  campaign  absolutely represents the best of our  country when do you think that vote  might happen then you know  well we are honestly hoping that the  conservative  government dig deep and look  introspectively  and perform a u-turn on this but we  certainly will be pushing for a vote  before christmas okay okay i'm keen to  talk to you about another story that's  emerged on the program today as well  we heard from bernard jenkin at the  beginning of the show calling  on dido harding the head of test and  trace to go  do you think it's time for new  leadership there look it's very  interesting i think  the huge take-home message here is that  the  the tories are infighting because even  they themselves can see  just how catastrophic the handling of  our test trace and isolate system  has been i mean should she go then do  you think it's time for her to go  well actually i think the real message  is about the people who are needing this  to work for them  we are seeing serco lining the pockets  of shareholders with 165 million pounds  of profit but not delivering the contact  racing we have been calling for as  labour party  for it to be in the hands of local  public health teams who have been  delivering a contact racing rate of 97.1  whereas circo if they're lucky get 68.1  it's time to put it back  to the local communities that know their  communities the new leadership then  her position is very difficult it's  untenable really but  fundamentally this comes down to the  responsibility of the government they  have  failed people and there are people who  are going into this christmas period  not knowing whether they're going to be  able to hug their elderly parent in a  care home  for the last time or not we need to be  speaking up for them  and for that we need to put it back into  the hands  of our local public health teams now i'm  keen to talk to you about  labour's own plan you want to see the  circuit breaker  a sort of short sharp lockdown to try  and drive down cases  so what i want to know about is the exit  strategy  would that be time limited or would you  be driven by the data  so we are calling for a short two to  three week circuit breaker because we  believe that ultimately  based on sage advice it would save lives  and be mostly  i know i understand why you're calling  for it what i'm trying to work out is  what is the exit strategy would you  would it last for a certain amount of  time no matter what happens  or would you be driven by the data no it  would last for a certain amount of time  no matter what happens and then we would  go back into the tiered system  okay i just want to have a look at what  kia stanley said at prime minister's  questions this week  he said this to the prime minister he  said is the prime minister seriously  saying  he would take a tier three area out of  tier three  with the r8 above one i don't think so  now are you seriously saying that you  would end  a circuit breaker lockdown if the r  remains above one because  i don't think you do that either we're  very clear that the circuit breaker  would be for a prescribed period of time  it would not be for a protracted period  of time  fundamentally this circuit breaker is  needed in order to get on top of the  shambolic test trace and isolate system  if we are able to get on top of that it  will protect our economy and although we  are not  and if the r8 remains above one you're  saying that you would just lift the  restrictions even though kia starman  doesn't believe boris johnson when he  says the same thing  we're very clear that the circuit  breaker would be  for a two to three week period only and  even the imf has said that if the  government don't take that advice and  don't act and do that now i mean look we  wanted it now over the half term period  when it would cause the least disruption  to people but it could cost our economy  110 billion pounds  the government have been asleep at the  wheel they have to act okay  i'm keen to ask about another story  around today we asked brandon uh lewis  about it too  about reviews reports that the  government is looking at bringing down  the south isolation period  from two weeks to potentially ten days  or even seven days  do you think that's a good idea i've  always been very clear from the start of  this pandemic especially with my work on  the front line how important it  is that we follow the science and we  follow the world health organization  advice on how long we should be self  isolating this is in order  to protect ourselves our families but  also more importantly everybody else  around us  and the british public have been  incredible they have shown such resolve  this has been going on for seven months  now  and the british public are tired and  they need hope but  it is only well it is essential that we  only do  what is safe and fundamentally it all  comes back down to getting on top of  test tracing isolate because if the  government were able to do that then  people would have some certainty  and there is nothing to say that if they  brought down the period to seven days  that people then wouldn't go out  off after three days so actually don't  think it'd have an impact on compliance  anyway  i think people are tired people are  tired and they need hope and they're  going into  a long dark winter we know that in the  first  phase of covid when when we had the  first peak  the ons figures showed that that  depression rates  um just just skyrocketed and  we have to understand that people have  been doing their best the majority of  the public have been doing their best  and i'm really proud of the public i'm  really proud of the british people  who are putting other people's safety  first as well as their own you're  talking about depression rates about the  long dark winter  it's so many of our viewers will be  feeling pretty down let's be frank  about the months to come um lockdown  self-isolation and social distancing all  taking its toll  how concerned are you by reports that  referrals to mental health services have  actually been dropping  i'm deeply concerned because i know that  that is not reflective of what we are  seeing at large and i would just like to  take this opportunity to say that the  nhs  are working incredibly hard they are  doing  their best and actually like mental ill  health  doesn't just doesn't discriminate it  doesn't know class it doesn't know  gender or  ethnicity and so many people have really  been struggling with their mental health  particularly our frontline nhs and care  workers which is why  labour called for a care for carers  package to put  their mental health first we know that  in june alone  32 of sickness days in the nhs was down  to mental ill health  i've raised this with the government  that that was more sickness days due to  mental ill health than to the  coronavirus itself but the government  just haven't been listening  the government need to have a plan in  place  a mental health and wellbeing strategy  going into this winter  that is what the labour party is calling  for they have to be gathering data  they need to be understanding where the  pressures are and they need to be  delivering for the people that need it  the most  isn't the problem though that for many  people the reason  they're suffering from mental ill health  is because they can't see people  they can't see their loved ones they  can't see their families  and does that not need to be taken into  account as well when we're thinking  about  imposing restrictions on people it needs  to be taken into account when we're  looking at the fact that test tracing  isolate has failed people because if  we'd got on top of that  it would have been so much easier i  understand why  your criticism is of test stress and  isolate but even if you look at someone  like germany for example whose test  tracing isolate system has been  praised their rate is about the same as  ours cases are going up it's  you can't blame the whole thing on test  tracking nicely do we not need to have a  wider conversation  about the impact that restrictions are  having on people's mental health  you're absolutely correct there are  people in some parts of the country  who've pretty much been in lockdown  since march  this government haven't managed to to  actually get on top of the virus  during that time which is why we're  calling for a short  two to three week circuit breaker to get  on top of the virus to drive the r  number down  and to give the government a chance to  fix test trace and isolate and we want  to  we want to work with the government to  make this happen it's in all of our  interests  but the british people are incredible  and they need hope and they need to know  that  they will get out the other side we will  get to next year and things will get  better but we just have to hold on to  that hope and know  that the government are doing all they  can to protect our mental health  and just finally you've recently been  fined  a thousand pounds just over a thousand  pounds for breaching  house of commons rules after you sent  out letters  saying that you were fighting brexit on  house of commons head of paper  prepaid envelopes during the election  campaign now  this is the third time you've breached  the rules in three years are you  becoming a bit of a serial offender here  no look the rules are important and they  are there to be followed the  the first time i broke the rules was  because on on paper that i paid for  myself  i used i used a picture of a crown port  collis i made a mistake i didn't i  didn't realize that that that wasn't  mistaken i then i then um  i declared my nhs payment for my shift a  little bit late  and i used i used paper  to respond to people who'd written to me  about brexit i did it in good faith i  held up my hands and said i'm sorry i  made a mistake  i'm human i'm not a career politician  but rules are there to be followed and  actually when i  realized that i'd made a mistake i  i straight away offered to repay the the  vm cost of the stationery and yeah i'm  sorry and i hold my hands up

